                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Producing accusations; in a manner that reflects a finding of fault or blame"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6f08ad6-a5a2-40ce-9305-bad099f7d558",
                                                "sense_id": "dae998a2-ee30-30fe-b364-6e8d3099952e",
                                                "text": "This hath been a very accusative age."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0169832-daf1-40b8-b93c-a09794dfba5b",
                                                "sense_id": "dae998a2-ee30-30fe-b364-6e8d3099952e",
                                                "text": "The proprietor of the store was rude, insulting and accusative."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c1ba571-b27c-3cfc-80d6-d85f3a1ad8e5",
                                        "entry_id": "d06a0bee-291f-32f7-afd1-1c1e8ece532a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Applied to the case (as the fourth case of Latin, Lithuanian and Greek nouns) which expresses the immediate object on which the action or influence of a transitive verb has its limited influence. Other parts of speech, including secondary or predicate direct objects, will also influence a sentence’s construction. In German the case used for direct objects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
